ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study uses colon cancer cases and controls from two previously described study populations: a multi-center population-based case-control study focusing on Diet, Activity and Lifestyle (DALS) and colon cancer [34] and a nested case-control study of colon cancer within the Women's Health Initiative (WHI) Observational Study [35-38].") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21129217") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0000569)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Japan Multi-institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) study was launched in 2005 to examine gene-environment interactions in lifestyle-related diseases, including cancers, among the Japanese.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:32963210") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle factors in gene-environment interactions") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0000571)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The QSkin Sun and Health Study comprises a cohort of 43 794 men and women aged 40-69 years randomly sampled from the population of Queensland, Australia in 2011. The cohort was established to study the development of skin cancer and melanoma in the population with the highest reported incidence of these diseases in the world. At baseline, besides demographic items and general medical history, information about standard pigmentary characteristics (including hair and eye colour, freckling tendency, tanning ability and propensity to sunburn), past and recent history of sun exposure and sunburns, sun protection behaviours, use of tanning beds and history of skin cancer was collected by self-completed questionnaire.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:22933644") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "sun exposure and sunburns") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000061) coho:COHO_0000574)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "What started as a project on diet and health among women, has over the years developed to include a male cohort, repeated assessments of diet and lifestyle factors, and repeated matching with national, regional, and local registers, in addition to sampling of clinical variables and biological samples.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.simpler4health.se/w/sh/en/about-us") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000577)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shanghai Men's Health Study (SMHS) is a population-based cohort study of 61,480 men aged 40-74 years, launched in 2002 in urban Shanghai to investigate the contribution of lifestyle/environmental factors and genetic susceptibility to cancer and other non-communicable diseases (NCDs).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25733578") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle/environmental factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0000578)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Vitamin and mineral supplements are among the most commonly used drugs in the United States, despite limited evidence on their benefits or risks. This paper describes the design, implementation, and participant characteristics of the VITamins And Lifestyle (VITAL) Study, a cohort study of the associations of supplement use with cancer risk.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:36404465") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9835888/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "vitamin and mineral supplement use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0070245) coho:COHO_0000579)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VITamins And Lifestyle (VITAL) cohort comprises 77,721 Washington State men and women aged 50 to 76 years, recruited from 2000 to 2002 to investigate the association of supplement use and lifestyle factors with cancer risk.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25105248") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0000579)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-cohort study aims to investigate how genetic and potentially modifiable lifestyle and behavioural factors, particularly diet and physical activity, interact in their influence on the risk of developing type 2 diabetes.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21717116") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle and behavioural factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0000587)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-cohort study aims to investigate how genetic and potentially modifiable lifestyle and behavioural factors, particularly diet and physical activity, interact in their influence on the risk of developing type 2 diabetes.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21717116") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000587)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-cohort study aims to investigate how genetic and potentially modifiable lifestyle and behavioural factors, particularly diet and physical activity, interact in their influence on the risk of developing type 2 diabetes.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21717116") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0000587)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swiss Cohort Study on Air Pollution and Lung Diseases in Adults (SAPALDIA) was designed to investigate the health effects from long-term exposure to air pollution.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:16167509") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "long-term exposure to air pollution") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "nitrogen dioxide (NO2), sulphur dioxide (SO2), ozone (O3) and particulates in ambient air") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000036) coho:COHO_0000589)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "carcinogenic heterocyclic amines (HA), which are produced by meat cooked at high temperatures and are found in cigarette smoke. A study of 500 incident colorectal cancer cases and population controls, matched for age, sex and general practitioner, was conducted in the UK to investigate this hypothesis.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:12584178") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "meat intake") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000596)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "carcinogenic heterocyclic amines (HA), which are produced by meat cooked at high temperatures and are found in cigarette smoke. A study of 500 incident colorectal cancer cases and population controls, matched for age, sex and general practitioner, was conducted in the UK to investigate this hypothesis.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:12584178") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cigarette smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000038) coho:COHO_0000596)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "carcinogenic heterocyclic amines (HA), which are produced by meat cooked at high temperatures and are found in cigarette smoke. A study of 500 incident colorectal cancer cases and population controls, matched for age, sex and general practitioner, was conducted in the UK to investigate this hypothesis.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:12584178") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "heterocyclic amines from meat cooked at high temperatures") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9000203) coho:COHO_0000596)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, ATBC was a randomized placebo‐controlled trial (NCT00342992 clinicaltrials.gov) examining α‐tocopherol and/or β‐carotene for primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male Finnish smokers, aged 50–69 years at recruitment between 1985 and 1988.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:40401725") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cigarette smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000038) coho:COHO_0000598)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CHNS was designed to provide representation of rural, urban, and suburban areas varying substantially in geography, economic development, public resources, and health indicators with a focus on examining household- and individual-level sociodemographic factors, diet, physical activity, health, and behavior changes relative to community-level urbanicity and social, and economic change.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24341753") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000630)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CHNS was designed to provide representation of rural, urban, and suburban areas varying substantially in geography, economic development, public resources, and health indicators with a focus on examining household- and individual-level sociodemographic factors, diet, physical activity, health, and behavior changes relative to community-level urbanicity and social, and economic change.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24341753") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0000630)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Exposure assessments comprise respiratory, intestinal, and skin microbiology; the child's diet; indoor and outdoor air quality; allergens; and indicators of lifestyle.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15521375") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "the child's diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000639)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the relationships among genetic, environmental, and lifestyle factors in the development of atopic diseases in high-risk children with the aim of developing evidence-based prevention strategies.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15521375") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental and lifestyle factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000639)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SPIROMICS study is a multicenter study that includes current and former smokers (≥ 20 pack years) with or without airflow obstruction and healthy participants who were non-smokers aged 40 to 80 years recruited from 12 clinical sites spread across the United States.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33906617") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "current and former smokers (≥ 20 pack years)") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000038) coho:COHO_0000652)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Measurements of environmental exposures include levels of house dust mite; cat and dog allergens during pregnancy and early life; pet ownership and exposure; childcare arrangements; number of siblings; vaccination uptake; thorough dietary questionnaire; and endotoxin exposure.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:12688622") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "house dust mite; cat and dog allergens during pregnancy and early life") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0900047) coho:COHO_0000656)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Measurements of environmental exposures include levels of house dust mite; cat and dog allergens during pregnancy and early life; pet ownership and exposure; childcare arrangements; number of siblings; vaccination uptake; thorough dietary questionnaire; and endotoxin exposure.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:12688622") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "endotoxin exposure") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9000215) coho:COHO_0000656)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "SCHS is a long-term population-based prospective cohort study focused on the dietary, genetic and environmental determinants of cancer and other chronic diseases in Singapore9.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35927272") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000659)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "SCHS is a long-term population-based prospective cohort study focused on the dietary, genetic and environmental determinants of cancer and other chronic diseases in Singapore9.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35927272") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental determinants of cancer and other chronic diseases") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000659)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Sister Study was designed to address concerns that not enough was being done to evaluate the impact of widespread environmental exposure to chemicals on trends in breast cancer incidence.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:29373861") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental exposure to chemicals") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0000931) coho:COHO_0000660)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Sister Study was designed to address concerns that not enough was being done to evaluate the impact of widespread environmental exposure to chemicals on trends in breast cancer incidence.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:29373861") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental risk factors for breast cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000660)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Evidence for other lifestyle habits, such as fluid intake and micturition, physical activity, and fruit and vegetable consumption, is very limited or not available.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31619424") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "fruit and vegetable consumption") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0070232) coho:COHO_0000661)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main aim of this study is to evaluate whether lifestyle habits are related to prognosis and HRQOL in patients with NMIBC.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31619424") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle habits") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0000661)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Evidence for other lifestyle habits, such as fluid intake and micturition, physical activity, and fruit and vegetable consumption, is very limited or not available.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31619424") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0000661)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "EGEA is a unique 20-year cohort set up to investigate the genetic and environmental factors and their interactions in asthma and asthma-related phenotypes (bronchial hyperresponsiveness, atopy), and to clarify the phenotypic heterogeneity [1, 2].") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "DOI:10.5334/ojb.24") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000664)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "COPDGene, COGEND, and ECLIPSE are all smoking cohorts and ratios of COPD were consistent across array and WGS datasets, thus we expected no genome-wide significant association signals (controlled type 1 error).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35953715") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0000706)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "GINIplus – The German Infant Study on the Influence of Nutrition Intervention plus Air pollution and Genetics on Allergy Development GINIplus is a prospective population-based birth cohort study.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30402607") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "Nutrition Intervention") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_2000068) coho:COHO_0000708)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "GINIplus – The German Infant Study on the Influence of Nutrition Intervention plus Air pollution and Genetics on Allergy Development GINIplus is a prospective population-based birth cohort study.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30402607") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "Air pollution") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000036) coho:COHO_0000708)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Herein, we report the first GWAS of common genetic variation for lung cancer and smoking phenotypes in 1737 African American cases and 3602 controls, followed by a replication phase including an independent set of 866 cases and 796 controls.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:27393504") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking phenotypes") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000038) coho:COHO_0000717)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nicotine dependent cases and non-dependent smoking controls were identified and recruited from Detroit and St. Louis.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35953715") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0000727)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AHS is a prospective cohort that includes 57,310 licensed pesticide applicators enrolled in Iowa or North Carolina between 1993 and 1997.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:38381478") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "pesticide use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_0000530) coho:COHO_0000740)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AHS is a prospective cohort that includes 57,310 licensed pesticide applicators enrolled in Iowa or North Carolina between 1993 and 1997.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:38381478") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "agricultural practices") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_1000034) coho:COHO_0000740)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Agricultural Lung Health Study (ALHS) is a case-control study of current asthma among farmers and their spouses nested within the prospective Agricultural Health Study (AHS data releases P3REL201209.00, PIREL201209.00 and AHSREL201304.00)") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:36914875") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10011137/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "farm exposures") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_1000034) coho:COHO_0000741)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Danish National Birth Cohort (DNBC) was established to investigate the causal link between exposures in early life and disease later on and the possibilities for disease prevention.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.dnbc.dk/about-the-dnbc") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "exposures in early life") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000748)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "We designed a large population-based case-control study that combines a traditional molecular epidemiology design with a more integrative approach to investigate the dynamic process that begins with smoking initiation, proceeds through dependency/smoking persistence, continues with lung cancer development and ends with progression to disseminated disease or response to therapy and survival.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18538025") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0000749)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants range in age from 7 to 97, with many having longitudinal assessments, providing a valuable opportunity to study alcohol use and problems across the lifespan.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:37581339") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0001082) coho:COHO_0000772)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "GEMS and EIMS are nationwide case-control studies examining the genetic and environmental risk factors for prevalent and incident MS, respectively.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:38630618") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental exposures and lifestyle factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000777)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were from a population-based cohort entitled the Nutrition and Health of Aging People in China (NHAPC) study, which was designed to investigate environmental and genetic factors and their interactions on cardiometabolic diseases [21,22].") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:34208976") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000789)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls are defined as individuals who have been exposed to alcohol (and possibly to other drugs), but have never met lifetime diagnosis for alcohol dependence or dependence on other illicit substances.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000092.v1.p1") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_9000026) coho:COHO_0000793)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "GALA II and SAGE are two clinic-based case-control studies focused on untangling the genetic and environmental basis of childhood-onset asthma disease in minority ethnic groups of the United States of America [22].") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:34834492") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental basis of childhood-onset asthma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0000794)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected on lifetime smoking, coffee drinking, dietary habits and lifetime occupation, with particular reference to exposure to aromatic amines (AAs) and polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24722645") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifetime smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000029) coho:COHO_0000815)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected on lifetime smoking, coffee drinking, dietary habits and lifetime occupation, with particular reference to exposure to aromatic amines (AAs) and polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24722645") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "occupational exposure to aromatic amines (AAs)") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9000203) coho:COHO_0000815)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected on lifetime smoking, coffee drinking, dietary habits and lifetime occupation, with particular reference to exposure to aromatic amines (AAs) and polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24722645") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "occupational exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs)") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9000433) coho:COHO_0000815)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "We hypothesize that perinatal exposures, in particular the human microbiome and maternal nutrition during pregnancy, interact with the genetic predisposition to cause an abnormal immune modulation in early life towards a trajectory to chronic inflammatory diseases such as asthma and others.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24118234") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "maternal nutrition during pregnancy") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_2000076) coho:COHO_0000819)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "COSM is a longitudinal, population-based study designed to study associations of lifestyle with morbidity and mortality") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33723363") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0000820)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The general aim of the study is to assess a wide range of modifiable lifestyle factors (diet, dietary supplements, physical activity, smoking, alcohol, body weight and other anthropometric measures, etc.) and genetic factors in a large population-based longitudinal cohort of Swedish middle-aged and elderly men.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.maelstrom-research.org/study/cosm") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0000820)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the entire cohort and subcohort, a GIS environment for the nine study areas was constructed, and, based on residential address histories, exposure estimates were assigned for ambient air pollutants, road traffic noise levels, surrounding (natural spaces green and blue spaces), built environment, ultraviolet (UV) radiation and meteorological variables during pregnancy and childhood (table 3).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "ultraviolet (UV) radiation") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0000006) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biomarkers include: organochlorine compounds and brominated compounds, perfluoroalkyl substances and metals in blood, and non-persistent chemicals (phthalate metabolites, phenols, organophosphate pesticide metabolites and cotinine) in urine samples (table 3).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "organochlorine compounds and brominated compounds") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0001152) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the entire cohort and subcohort, a GIS environment for the nine study areas was constructed, and, based on residential address histories, exposure estimates were assigned for ambient air pollutants, road traffic noise levels, surrounding (natural spaces green and blue spaces), built environment, ultraviolet (UV) radiation and meteorological variables during pregnancy and childhood (table 3).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "meteorological variables") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_1000020) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Tobacco smoking Urine levels of cotinine. Questionnaire on active and passive smoking.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "tobacco smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000029) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Intensive repeat panel studies collected data on short-term temporal variability in exposure biomarkers and omics biomarkers, individual behaviours (physical activity, mobility) and personal and indoor exposures (table 5).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Existing data included information on certain exposures (eg, maternal tobacco smoking during pregnancy, environmental tobacco smoke), key covariates (eg, pregnancy complications, maternal and child diet, maternal and child physical activity, child sleep, breast feeding, other health-related behaviours, indicators of socioeconomic status) and health and development outcomes.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental tobacco smoke") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_7000059) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Concentrations of drinking water disinfection by-products (DBPs) during pregnancy were estimated from water company concentration and distribution data as part of the water contaminants and stillbirth, congenital anomalies, birth weight, preterm delivery (HiWate) project in four of the cohorts (BiB, KANC, INMA, RHEA).38 For EDEN and MoBa, we followed the same methodology to obtain estimates during pregnancy.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "drinking water disinfection by-products") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_7000125) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the entire cohort and subcohort, a GIS environment for the nine study areas was constructed, and, based on residential address histories, exposure estimates were assigned for ambient air pollutants, road traffic noise levels, surrounding (natural spaces green and blue spaces), built environment, ultraviolet (UV) radiation and meteorological variables during pregnancy and childhood (table 3).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "ambient air pollutants") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000036) coho:COHO_0000827)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the entire cohort and subcohort, a GIS environment for the nine study areas was constructed, and, based on residential address histories, exposure estimates were assigned for ambient air pollutants, road traffic noise levels, surrounding (natural spaces green and blue spaces), built environment, ultraviolet (UV) radiation and meteorological variables during pregnancy and childhood (table 3).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30206078") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "road traffic noise levels") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000044) coho:COHO_0000827)
