ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Santiago Longitudinal Study (SLS) is a cohort of participants recruited from community clinics in Santiago, Chile, at infancy between 1991 and 1996 for participation in a randomized trial of iron supplementation to prevent iron deficiency anemia") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:39885687") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "iron supplementation in infancy") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_2000097) coho:COHO_0001407)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SLS began September 1992 to study the effects of nutrition on children’s health, with follow-up assessments at ages 1, 5, 10, 12, 14, 16, 19, 21, 23, and 29 years.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SLS") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "nutrition") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9001695) coho:COHO_0001407)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Singapore Preconception Study of Long-Term Maternal and Child Outcomes (S-PRESTO) is a preconception, longitudinal cohort study that aims to study the effects of nutrition, lifestyle, and maternal mood prior to and during pregnancy on the epigenome of the offspring") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33222050") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "nutrition prior to and during pregnancy") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_2000076) coho:COHO_0001413)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Singapore Preconception Study of Long-Term Maternal and Child Outcomes (S-PRESTO) is a preconception, longitudinal cohort study that aims to study the effects of nutrition, lifestyle, and maternal mood prior to and during pregnancy on the epigenome of the offspring") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33222050") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001413)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The strengths of S-PRESTO are the objective assessment of body composition by imaging as well as assessment of environmental factors via collection of household dust and skin samples since preconception, allowing the determination of environmental microbiome and its influence on host microbiome, dysbiosis of which leads to disease development.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33222050") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental factors assessed via household dust and skin samples") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0001413)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "(2) determine environmental risk factors (diet, lifestyle, occupational) and life-course causes of common chronic diseases which are emerging with the economic development of China;") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19589173") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "occupational") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0001591) coho:COHO_0001426)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TZL study is focused on exploring the multiple environmental and lifestyles exposures altered during the process of economic transformation of China, solely or in combination with multiple genetic factors, on the gradually increased prevalence of non-communicable chronic diseases.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19589173") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001426)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main objectives of the TZL study are to: (1) describe the mortality and morbidity characteristics of common chronic diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, diabetes mellitus, and cancers; (2) determine environmental risk factors (diet, lifestyle, occupational) and life-course causes of common chronic diseases which are emerging with the economic development of China; (3) determine genetic risk factors underlying common chronic diseases; and (4) determine the contribution of gene-environment interactions to the common chronic diseases.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19589173") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001426)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TZL study is focused on exploring the multiple environmental and lifestyles exposures altered during the process of economic transformation of China, solely or in combination with multiple genetic factors, on the gradually increased prevalence of non-communicable chronic diseases.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19589173") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental and lifestyle exposures altered during economic transformation") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0001426)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility in the etiology of breast cancer, we designed a case-control study nested within five population-based cancer registries.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15084244") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "radiation exposure") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0000001) coho:COHO_0001434)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility in the etiology of breast cancer, we designed a case-control study nested within five population-based cancer registries. We hypothesized that a woman carrying a mutant allele in one of these genes is more susceptible to radiation-induced breast cancer than is a non-carrier. In our study, 700 women with asynchronous bilateral breast cancer were individually matched to 1400 controls with unilateral breast cancer on date and age at diagnosis of the first breast cancer, race, and registry region, and counter-matched on radiation therapy. Each triplet comprised two women who received radiation therapy and one woman who did not. Radiation absorbed dose to the contralateral breast after initial treatment was estimated with a comprehensive dose reconstruction approach that included experimental measurements in anthropomorphic and water phantoms applying patient treatment parameters.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15084244") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "radiation absorbed dose to the contralateral breast after radiation therapy") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_2000079) coho:COHO_0001434)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In response to this need, the International Cannabis Consortium was established to combine the results of multiple GWASs to identify the genetic variants underlying individual differences in cannabis use phenotypes.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:27023175") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifetime cannabis use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0100005) coho:COHO_0001439)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Figure 2: Forest plots of odds ratios and 95% confidence intervals for the susceptibility loci for alcohol-related cirrhosis in comparison to alcohol misusers and population controls.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26482880") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol misuse") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol misuse") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000009) coho:COHO_0001467)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Arsenic Health Risk Assessment and Molecular Epidemiology (ASHRAM) study aimed to quantify the risks of several cancer types in relation to long-term low-level iAs exposure via drinking water in Hungary, Romania, and Slovakia.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:22436128") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "inorganic arsenic in drinking water") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0080000) coho:COHO_0001497)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Throughout the entire period of the study half the families, selected at random, were supplied with milk tokens entitling the mother, while pregnant, and all children under age 5 years, to 1 pint of milk a day at half its current price.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:7030223") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "milk supplementation in pregnancy and early childhood") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0070204) coho:COHO_0001517)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Bangladesh Vitamin E and Selenium Trial (BEST) [28] was established in Araihazar and surrounding areas in 2006 to determine whether 7,000 arsenic-exposed participants who supplemented their diet with vitamin E and selenium would reduce their rate of non-melanoma skin cancer.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25133637") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "arsenic exposure") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_9000032) coho:COHO_0001524)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "By use of a whole-population ascertainment scheme, 822 individuals were enrolled from a schistosomiasis-endemic area in Conde, Bahia, in Brazil.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18717640") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "residence in a Schistosoma mansoni-endemic area") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_3000174) coho:COHO_0001529)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Together with the inclusion of genetic, epigenetic, and neuroendocrine measures, this makes it possible to explore the interplay between biological and environmental factors in the development of mental health and wellbeing outcomes in children exposed to war and adversity associated with being a refugee.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35041012") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "war and adversity associated with being a refugee") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "civilian exposure to war events") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000001) coho:COHO_0001533)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the association between occupational exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, aromatic amines and diesel and bladder cancer risk and the modification by smoking and metabolic polymorphisms, have we recruited 200 cases and 385 population controls.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:16504378") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0001547)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the association between occupational exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, aromatic amines and diesel and bladder cancer risk and the modification by smoking and metabolic polymorphisms, have we recruited 200 cases and 385 population controls.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:16504378") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "occupational exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, aromatic amines and diesel") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9000433) coho:COHO_0001547)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "It includes the nested case-control samples from 3 screening programs: IELCAP- Toronto: Ever smokers of more than 10 pack-years age 50 and above were eligible for the I-ELCAP screening program since 2003, and a total of 4782 individuals have been enrolled in the Greater Toronto Area.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:28604730") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0001563)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Intervention measures included avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergen, and environmental tobacco smoke.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15100668") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "pet allergen") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0000726) coho:COHO_0001565)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast-feeding was encouraged with formula supplementation if necessary, and introduction of solid foods was delayed.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15100668") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "breast-feeding and delayed introduction of solid foods") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0070224) coho:COHO_0001565)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Intervention measures included avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergen, and environmental tobacco smoke.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15100668") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "house dust mite allergen") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0900047) coho:COHO_0001565)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Intervention measures included avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergen, and environmental tobacco smoke.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15100668") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental tobacco smoke") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_7000059) coho:COHO_0001565)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "CARET is a multicenter, two-armed, double-masked randomized chemoprevention trial in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Baltimore, Connecticut, and Irvine, to test whether oral administration of beta-carotene (30 mg/day) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU/day) can decrease the incidence of lung cancer in high risk populations, namely, heavy smokers and asbestos-exposed workers.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:8137335") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "heavy smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000029) coho:COHO_0001571)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "CARET is a multicenter, two-armed, double-masked randomized chemoprevention trial in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Baltimore, Connecticut, and Irvine, to test whether oral administration of beta-carotene (30 mg/day) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU/day) can decrease the incidence of lung cancer in high risk populations, namely, heavy smokers and asbestos-exposed workers.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:8137335") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "occupational asbestos exposure") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_9000033) coho:COHO_0001571)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CEFALO study is a multinational case–control study conducted in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, with the primary aim to investigate the possible association between CABT risk and mobile phone use and other relevant exposures (Aydin et al, 2011).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23652309") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "mobile phone use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000054) coho:COHO_0001584)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ChooseWell 365 study will determine if an automated, personalized worksite intervention to nudge healthier choices improves overall diet and cardiometabolic health.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30414448") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "workplace cafeteria food choices") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001591)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Southern California Children’s Health Study (CHS) was designed to investigate the chronic effects of air pollution on respiratory health.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:20371422") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "regional ambient air pollution") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "air pollution") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_8000036) coho:COHO_0001592)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both men and women between the ages of 18 and 80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence based on DSM-IV-TR criteria with the last drink 5 or more days before enrollment were included in the study.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25290263") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol dependence (heavy alcohol use)") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000009) coho:COHO_0001595)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The identification of behavioral factors affecting prognosis and response to treatment is a research area ColoCare is designed to address through a series of surveys that include key health behavior research questions related to potentially modifiable exposures such as physical activity, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) use, alcohol consumption, dietary factors, and many more.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30523039") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol consumption") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0001082) coho:COHO_0001604)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of the ColoCare Study is to provide the research infrastructure needed to identify new biologic markers (e.g., metabolomic, transcriptomic, metagenomic, genetic, epigenetic, and proteomic biomarkers) that predict clinical outcomes, and to characterize associations between potentially modifiable risk factors (e.g., diet, supplement use, NSAID use, physical activity, body composition, etc.) with short-term and long-term patient-reported and clinical outcomes (e.g., therapy-induced toxicities, recurrence, survival and quality of life, etc.) among patients with colorectal cancer.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30523039") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "dietary supplement use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0070245) coho:COHO_0001604)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The identification of behavioral factors affecting prognosis and response to treatment is a research area ColoCare is designed to address through a series of surveys that include key health behavior research questions related to potentially modifiable exposures such as physical activity, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) use, alcohol consumption, dietary factors, and many more.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30523039") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "dietary factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001604)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The identification of behavioral factors affecting prognosis and response to treatment is a research area ColoCare is designed to address through a series of surveys that include key health behavior research questions related to potentially modifiable exposures such as physical activity, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) use, alcohol consumption, dietary factors, and many more.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30523039") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0001604)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "We extensively investigate diet and lifestyle of colorectal cancer patients at diagnosis and during the following years; this design paper focusses on the initial exposures of interest: diet and dietary supplement use, body composition, nutrient status (e.g. vitamin D), and composition of the gut microbiota.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24886284") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "dietary supplement use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0070245) coho:COHO_0001605)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main aim of this study is to assess associations of diet and other lifestyle factors, with colorectal cancer recurrence, survival and quality of life.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24886284") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001605)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, COPACETIC only recruited heavy smokers and we could therefore not assess the effects of the 15q24/25 locus in subjects being exposed to less nicotine.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23349703") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "heavy smoking (at least 20 pack-years)") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000029) coho:COHO_0001622)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of the cohort is to investigate associations of diet and lifestyle with the risk of cancer and other chronic diseases.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:36852012") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001650)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of the cohort is to investigate associations of diet and lifestyle with the risk of cancer and other chronic diseases.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:36852012") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001650)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "DietCompLyf is a multi-centre prospective study designed to investigate associations between phytoestrogens - naturally occurring plant compounds with oestrogenic properties - and other diet and lifestyle factors with breast cancer recurrence and survival.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23664318") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet and lifestyle factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001667)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "DietCompLyf is a multi-centre prospective study designed to investigate associations between phytoestrogens - naturally occurring plant compounds with oestrogenic properties - and other diet and lifestyle factors with breast cancer recurrence and survival.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23664318") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "phytoestrogens") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9002037) coho:COHO_0001667)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Arsenic Health Risk Assessment and Molecular epidemiology study (ASHRAM), is a case–control study of cancer risks in relation to arsenic exposure via drinking water in areas of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:20401490") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "arsenic in drinking water") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0080000) coho:COHO_0001681)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ENGELA study is a French multicenter hospital-based case-control study that was conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004 in order to investigate for environmental, infectious and genetics risk factors for LN.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19058175") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental risk factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0001689)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Certain professions (farmers, professional users of pesticides, food or rubber industry workers, medical workers, night watchers…) and certain working hours (night work, rotating shift work) are more specifically documented using specific occupational questionnaires.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24552491") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "night work") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "rotating shift work") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0001591) coho:COHO_0001692)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In contrast, the study will well serve the postulated main aim, to investigate gene–lifestyle interactions in the causation of common diseases in the middle-aged and elderly, since this only requires sufficiently large ranges in the distributions of lifestyle factors and genetic variants.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23435790") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001697)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present hospital‐based case‐only study was conducted on the basis of a case‐control study named as EPI‐NPC‐2005 project conducted during October 2005 and October 2007, which was designed to assess the interaction between EBV, environmental factors and genetic determinants in the pathogenesis and progression of NPC.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31241250") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "EBV") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_3000273) coho:COHO_0001699)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present hospital‐based case‐only study was conducted on the basis of a case‐control study named as EPI‐NPC‐2005 project conducted during October 2005 and October 2007, which was designed to assess the interaction between EBV, environmental factors and genetic determinants in the pathogenesis and progression of NPC.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31241250") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0001699)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ESCALE study is a national study conducted in 2003 and 2004 in mainland France (11 million children < 15 years of age) to investigate the role of infectious, environmental, and genetic factors in four childhood neoplastic diseases (acute leukemia, lymphoma, neuroblastoma, and brain tumor) (Brosselin et al. 2009; Rudant et al. 2007, 2008, 2010).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21147599") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0001707)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "A case-control study was designed to elucidate roles of dietary and other behavioral influences, in combination with genetic susceptibility factors (genetic polymorphisms), in colorectal carcinogenesis.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:15546244") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001720)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main areas addressed are alcohol use and its consequences, smoking, physical activity, overall physical health, eating behaviors and eating disorders, weight development, obesity, life satisfaction and personality.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31796134") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "alcohol use") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0001082) coho:COHO_0001727)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main areas addressed are alcohol use and its consequences, smoking, physical activity, overall physical health, eating behaviors and eating disorders, weight development, obesity, life satisfaction and personality.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31796134") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0001727)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main areas addressed are alcohol use and its consequences, smoking, physical activity, overall physical health, eating behaviors and eating disorders, weight development, obesity, life satisfaction and personality.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31796134") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0001727)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since its establishment, the FTC has been hosted by the University of Helsinki and the primary goal in the 1970s and early 1980s was to study twin-pairs discordant for smoking, as the causal evidence for smoking in major diseases was still lacking.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31462340") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0001728)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall goal of this project is to identify and characterize genetic variants that contribute to the development of nicotine dependence, related smoking behaviors, and smoking cessation.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000404.v1.p1") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0001756)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the current study was to elucidate the joint role of the GSTP1 Ile105Val polymorphism and occupational exposures to PAH in prostate cancer.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17067754") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "occupational exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs)") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9000433) coho:COHO_0001765)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gene-Diet Attica Investigation on childhood obesity (GENDAI) evaluates the contributions to and pivotal interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity variables on children's weight.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17378724") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "dietary variables") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001774)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gene-Diet Attica Investigation on childhood obesity (GENDAI) evaluates the contributions to and pivotal interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity variables on children's weight.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17378724") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity variables") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0001774)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The \"GHRAS\" study is aimed at investigating the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological, and biochemical factors determining the health status of elderly Greeks.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18376349") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001801)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The \"GHRAS\" study is aimed at investigating the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological, and biochemical factors determining the health status of elderly Greeks.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18376349") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "dietary factors") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001801)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "With 4,545 cases and 4,173 controls, the GICC Study confers the opportunity to evaluate both environmental exposures and genetic variation while accounting for tumor subtype.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26656478") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "environmental exposures") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ExO_0000002) coho:COHO_0001803)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort will provide data that will be influential in establishing the role of nutrition in metabolic diseases with multi-omics.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:37813622") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "nutrition") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9001695) coho:COHO_0001817)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The measurements included blood pressure responses to the cold pressor stress test and to a high salt diet, triglyceride excursion in response to a high-fat challenge, and response in platelet aggregation to aspirin therapy.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18440328") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "high salt diet") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_0900473) coho:COHO_0001839)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The measurements included blood pressure responses to the cold pressor stress test and to a high salt diet, triglyceride excursion in response to a high-fat challenge, and response in platelet aggregation to aspirin therapy.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18440328") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "high-fat challenge") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_2000073) coho:COHO_0001839)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Assessing, understanding and modifying nutritional status, eating habits and physical activity in European adolescents: the HELENA (Healthy Lifestyle in Europe by Nutrition in Adolescence) Study.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17617932") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "eating habits") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000021) coho:COHO_0001852)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Assessing, understanding and modifying nutritional status, eating habits and physical activity in European adolescents: the HELENA (Healthy Lifestyle in Europe by Nutrition in Adolescence) Study.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17617932") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "physical activity") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000039) coho:COHO_0001852)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Assessing, understanding and modifying nutritional status, eating habits and physical activity in European adolescents: the HELENA (Healthy Lifestyle in Europe by Nutrition in Adolescence) Study.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17617932") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "nutritional status") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9001695) coho:COHO_0001852)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HELIAD is a population-based, multidisciplinary, collaborative study designed to estimate the prevalence and incidence of AD, other dementias, mild cognitive impairment, and other neuropsychiatric conditions of aging in the Greek population and to investigate associations between nutrition and cognitive dysfunction/age-related neuropsychiatric diseases in this Mediterranean population.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24993387") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "nutrition") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_9001695) coho:COHO_0001853)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HERITAGE family study (HEalth, RIsk factors, exercise Training And GEnetics) will document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic, and hormonal responses to aerobic exercise training.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:7674877") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "aerobic exercise training") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000002) coho:COHO_0001856)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our primary hypothesis was that in patients with stable heart failure, regular structured exercise training, when added to usual, evidence-based care in accordance with published guidelines, would significantly reduce the incidence of a combined end point of all-cause mortality or all-cause hospitalization.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19351941") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "regular structured exercise training") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000002) coho:COHO_0001857)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "All models were fit using data from a lung cancer study of 1275 cases and 1269 controls that has focused on gene-smoking relationships.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:16214908") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "smoking") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000013) coho:COHO_0001865)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study seeks to identify the factors important in the development of depression during medical internship and to utilize internship as a stress model to study subjects before and after the onset of a major stressor and assess the moderating effect of 5-HTTLPR on the development of depression.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:20368500") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "internship stress") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_participants_with_exposure obo:ECTO_0001591) coho:COHO_0001910)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "This gives us an unprecedented opportunity to probe the correlation, if any, between genetic and epigenetic changes in the genome and rapid changes in lifestyle.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23205164") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lifestyle") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_designed_to_study_exposure obo:ECTO_6000015) coho:COHO_0001919)
